{"item": 11, "topic": {"description": "How much residual-value/loss-share exposure has Nvidia taken on under its customer data center financing support — the commitment to cover up to 25% of the loss if financed chips lose value — and how much is disclosed at its next annual report?", "outcome": "The maximum potential amount of Nvidia's loss coverage on customer data center chip values, any amounts paid or accrued, and the terms and remaining duration of that support, as disclosed in Nvidia's next annual report.", "period": "Nvidia's next annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027), as fixed by the reason for an obligation already undertaken.", "settled_by": "Nvidia's next annual report (Form 10-K), including its guarantees and contingent-liability note and any related customer-financing disclosures."}, "answer": {"question": "What is Nvidia's maximum potential loss-coverage obligation, in USD, under its customer data center chip-value financing support at FY2027 year-end, as disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K guarantees, contingent-liability and related customer-financing disclosures?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "Amounts paid under the support", "why": "Payments are realized costs rather than the maximum potential loss-coverage obligation being tracked."}, {"part": "Amounts accrued under the support", "why": "Accrued liabilities are a separate accounting measure from the maximum potential loss-coverage obligation."}, {"part": "The commitment to cover up to 25% of losses", "why": "The coverage percentage is a contractual term, not the total dollar obligation being tracked."}, {"part": "Other terms of the support", "why": "Other contractual terms describe the arrangement but are not the tracked maximum dollar obligation."}, {"part": "Remaining duration of the support", "why": "Remaining duration is a separate contractual measure rather than the amount of potential loss coverage."}], "event": null, "figure": {"unit": "USD", "year": "FY2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "1000000000"}, {"lo": "1000000000", "hi": "5000000000"}, {"lo": "5000000000", "hi": "10000000000"}, {"lo": "10000000000", "hi": "20000000000"}, {"lo": "20000000000", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "lower", "favourable_why": "A lower maximum obligation limits Nvidia's potential losses from customer-financing support, whose demand benefits and financial risks the item both describe."}, "reference": null, "due_day": "2027-02-28", "due_day_basis": "expected_publication"}, "passage": null}
{"item": 12, "topic": {"description": "How much will NVIDIA disclose in purchase and supply commitments (obligations to buy capacity, components or services) at its next annual report?", "outcome": "The amount of purchase obligations/supply commitments NVIDIA reports in its contractual obligations and purchase commitment disclosures in the Form 10-K, versus the prior year, given the analyst report that NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments.", "period": "Fiscal 2027 annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027; Form 10-K expected around February 2027) — the next annual report after this 22 September 2026 item, per section 3 (an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report).", "settled_by": "NVIDIA's next Form 10-K (fiscal 2027), specifically its purchase obligations / contractual commitments disclosure and related notes."}, "answer": {"question": "What total amount in USD of outstanding purchase obligations and supply commitments to buy capacity, components or services will NVIDIA report at FY2027 year-end in its FY2027 Form 10-K contractual commitments disclosures and related notes, counting each obligation only once?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "Comparison with the prior year, including whether NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments.", "why": "The tracked outcome is the amount disclosed at FY2027 year-end, not its change from the prior year or a separate test of the analyst's characterization."}], "event": null, "figure": {"unit": "USD", "year": "FY2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "30000000000"}, {"lo": "30000000000", "hi": "60000000000"}, {"lo": "60000000000", "hi": "90000000000"}, {"lo": "90000000000", "hi": "120000000000"}, {"lo": "120000000000", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "lower", "favourable_why": "Lower commitments reduce NVIDIA's contractual purchasing exposure, and neither the topic nor the item establishes that a larger obligation is better for its business."}, "reference": null, "due_day": "2027-02-28", "due_day_basis": "expected_publication"}, "passage": null}
{"item": 13, "topic": {"description": "How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data centers in calendar 2027?", "outcome": "The big five AI hyperscalers' combined calendar-2027 data-center capital expenditure, versus the $1.3 trillion Nvidia projects for next year (as cited in the item) and the nearly $800 billion expected for calendar 2026.", "period": "Calendar year 2027, checked at the hyperscalers' 2027 capex guidance from their October 2026 earnings and at their Q4/full-year 2027 earnings and capex disclosures in early 2028.", "settled_by": "The five hyperscalers' calendar-2027 capital expenditure guidance in their quarterly earnings releases and their reported capex in Q4/full-year 2027 results and Form 10-Ks (early 2028)."}, "answer": {"question": "How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data-center capital expenditure in calendar 2027, as reported in their Q4/full-year 2027 results, capex disclosures and Form 10-Ks?", "object": "ai-capex", "not_judged": [{"part": "Calendar-2027 capex guidance issued during October 2026 earnings and subsequent quarterly releases.", "why": "Guidance is interim evidence, while the tracked outcome is actual combined calendar-2027 data-center capital expenditure."}, {"part": "Comparison with the nearly $800 billion expected for calendar 2026.", "why": "The prior-year comparison is context rather than the tracked calendar-2027 spending amount."}], "event": null, "figure": {"unit": "USD", "year": "2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "1000000000000"}, {"lo": "1000000000000", "hi": "1200000000000"}, {"lo": "1200000000000", "hi": "1400000000000"}, {"lo": "1400000000000", "hi": "1600000000000"}, {"lo": "1600000000000", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "n/a", "favourable_why": ""}, "reference": {"words": "the current estimates are for their capex to rise to $1.3 trillion next year. That's just according to Nvidia's projections", "kind": "expected", "value": "1300000000000", "value_to": n