{"item": 14, "topic": {"description": "How much will average DRAM (including HBM) contract prices rise in calendar 2026, as Nvidia reports substantially higher memory and component costs across the industry?", "outcome": "The change in average DRAM/HBM contract prices in calendar 2026 versus calendar 2025, per TrendForce/DRAMeXchange data.", "period": "Calendar year 2026 — the item's present-tense 'ongoing memory shortage' and Nvidia's statement that memory costs 'have increased substantially' (article dated 2 October 2026); checked against TrendForce/DRAMeXchange full-year 2026 DRAM contract price data (expected early 2027).", "settled_by": "TrendForce/DRAMeXchange quarterly DRAM and HBM contract price releases, and the quarterly results of memory makers SK Hynix, Micron and Samsung."}, "answer": {"question": "What is the percentage change in average DRAM contract prices, including HBM, in calendar 2026 versus calendar 2025, as reported in TrendForce/DRAMeXchange full-year contract price data?", "object": "semiconductor-cycle", "not_judged": [{"part": "Nvidia's report that memory and other component costs have increased substantially across the industry.", "why": "This is background evidence rather than the tracked annual change in average DRAM/HBM contract prices."}, {"part": "The ongoing memory shortage.", "why": "The shortage provides context but its persistence or severity is not the tracked price outcome."}], "event": null, "figure": {"unit": "percent", "year": "2026", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "0"}, {"lo": "0", "hi": "15"}, {"lo": "15", "hi": "30"}, {"lo": "30", "hi": "50"}, {"lo": "50", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "n/a", "favourable_why": ""}, "reference": null, "due_day": "2027-03-31", "due_day_basis": "expected_publication"}, "passage": null}
{"item": 15, "topic": {"description": "How much of Nvidia's $279 billion of supply and capacity commitments will remain outstanding or unconditional at its next annual report?", "outcome": "The total supply and capacity purchase commitments and the portion that is adjustable or cancelable at a cost, as disclosed in Nvidia's next annual report.", "period": "Nvidia's next annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027), as fixed by the reason for an obligation already undertaken.", "settled_by": "Nvidia's next annual report (Form 10-K), including the purchase obligations or commitments table."}, "answer": {"question": "What will Nvidia's total outstanding supply and capacity purchase commitments be at FY2027 year-end, as disclosed in the purchase obligations or commitments table and related notes in its FY2027 Form 10-K?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "The portion of commitments that is adjustable or cancelable at a cost.", "why": "This is a separate measure of contractual flexibility, rather than the total commitments tracked by the question."}, {"part": "The amount of commitments that is unconditional.", "why": "Unconditional commitments are a subset of the total and are not separately judged."}], "event": null, "figure": {"unit": "USD", "year": "FY2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "200000000000"}, {"lo": "200000000000", "hi": "250000000000"}, {"lo": "250000000000", "hi": "300000000000"}, {"lo": "300000000000", "hi": "350000000000"}, {"lo": "350000000000", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "lower", "favourable_why": "Lower commitments reduce Nvidia's exposure to purchase obligations that could become harder to absorb if customer spending slows."}, "reference": {"words": "Nvidia disclosed $279 billion of supply and capacity commitments across future fiscal years, some adjustable or cancelable at a cost.", "kind": "last_reported", "value": "279000000000", "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2027-02-28", "due_day_basis": "expected_publication"}, "passage": "Nvidia disclosed $279 billion of supply and capacity commitments across future fiscal years, some adjustable or cancelable at a cost."}
{"item": 16, "topic": {"description": "By how much will contract prices for AI-server memory (HBM/DRAM) — the memory input cost embedded in Nvidia's GPUs — rise or fall in calendar 2027?", "outcome": "The change in HBM/DRAM contract prices over calendar 2027, and the memory makers' reported average selling prices and memory gross margins for the periods covering 2027.", "period": "Calendar 2027 (overlapping Micron's fiscal 2027, roughly September 2026–August 2027), as supported by Micron management's fiscal 2027 price guidance in the October 6, 2026 article.", "settled_by": "TrendForce/DRAMeXchange monthly and quarterly memory contract price releases, together with the quarterly reports of Micron, SK Hynix and Samsung covering calendar 2027."}, "answer": {"question": "What is the calendar-2027 percentage change in AI-server HBM/DRAM contract prices, measured as the equal-weighted mean of the Q4 2027 versus Q4 2026 percentage changes for matched AI-server HBM and DRAM contract-price quotations in TrendForce/DRAMeXchange releases?", "object": "semiconductor-cycle", "not_judged": [{"part": "Memory makers' reported average selling prices for periods covering 2027.", "why": "Company-specific average selling prices reflect product mix and sales arrangements and are not the sector contract-price change being tracked."}, {"part": "Memory makers' reported memory gross margins for periods covering 2027.", "why": "Gross margins are a separate profitability measure rather than the tracked contract-price change."}, {"part": "The memory input cost embedded in Nvidia's GPUs.", "why": "Nvidia's realized input cost depends on its procurement arrangements and product mix and is not the sector contract-price measure."}, {"part": "The overlap with Micron's fiscal 2027 and its management's fiscal-2027 price guidance.", "why": "Micron's fiscal period and company-specific guidance provide context but do not determine the calendar-2027 sector price outcome."}], "event": null, "figure": {"unit": "percent", "year": "2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "-10"}, {"lo": "-10", "hi": "0"}, {"lo": "0", "hi": "10"}, {"lo": "10", "hi": "25"}, {"lo": "25", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "n/a", "favourable_why": ""}, "reference": null, "due_day": "2028-03-31", "due_day_basis": "expected_publication"}, "passage": null}
{"item": 17, "topic": {"description": "Will Nvidia complete its approximately $12.93 billion acquisition of Hugging Face — and at what final cost and regulatory conditions — by the check date?", "outcome": "Closing or termination of the signed Hugging Face acquisition, the final consideration paid (roughly $11.9 billion to shareholders plus up to $1 billion of equity-based retention awards), and any conditions regulators impose.", "period": "Check date: the first half of calendar 2027, the closing window the Sept. 3, 2026 agreement states (within 18 months of the Oct. 6, 2026 item).", "settled_by": "Nvidia's closing announcement and the regulatory (antitrust and any foreign-investment) clearance decisions, plus the purchase accounting and cash outflow disclosed in Nvidia's subsequent quarterly and annual filings."}, "answer": {"question": "Will Nvidia have completed its signed acquisition of Hugging Face by February 28, 2027, as established by its closing announcement or next annual filing?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "The final acquisition cost versus approximately $12.93 billion, including roughly $11.9 billion to shareholders and up to $1 billion in equity-based retention awards.", "why": "The judged event is completion of the acquisition, not the amount or composition of the final consideration."}, {"part": "Any regulatory conditions imposed on the acquisition.", "why": "Conditions attached to clearance do not constitute separate outcomes for whether the acquisition closes."}, {"part": "Completion during the remainder of the first half of calendar 2027 after the next annual filing.", "why": "The already-signed binding obligation is assessed at the next annual filing rather than at the end of the anticipated closing window."}], "event": {"happened": "Nvidia has consummated the Hugging Face acquisition by February 28, 2027, as confirmed by its closing announcement or annual filing.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia, Hugging Face, or an antitrust or foreign-investment authority with jurisdiction over the acquisition", "decision": "After October 6, 2026, Nvidia or Hugging Face formally terminates the acquisition agreement, or an antitrust or foreign-investment authority with jurisdiction issues a final decision prohibiting the acquisition as a whole."}}, "figure": null, "reference": {"words": "The closing of the transaction is subject to customary conditions and regulatory approvals and is anticipated to occur in the first half of 2027.", "kind": "expected", "value": null, "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2027-02-28", "due_day_basis": "stated"}, "passage": "The closing of the transaction is subject to customary conditions and regulatory approvals and is anticipated to occur in the first half of 2027."}
