{"item": 22, "topic": {"description": "Will NVIDIA complete its approximately $12.9 billion acquisition of Hugging Face, agreed in 2026, by the check date?", "outcome": "Whether the agreed ~$12.9 billion Hugging Face acquisition is signed and closed (completed) as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings, versus being repriced, delayed past the check date or terminated.", "period": "Check date 24 March 2028 (18 months after the 25 September 2026 item) — set per section 3 for a sized acquisition not yet completed, because the item gives no signing or closing date; also observable in NVIDIA's quarterly filings before then.", "settled_by": "NVIDIA's Form 8-K/press release announcing completion (or termination) of the Hugging Face acquisition, and the purchase-price and goodwill disclosures in its Form 10-Q/10-K."}, "answer": {"question": "Will NVIDIA have completed its agreed acquisition of Hugging Face by 28 February 2027, as established by its completion announcement, Form 8-K or quarterly or annual filings?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "The approximately $12.9 billion purchase price and whether the acquisition is repriced.", "why": "Completion is the tracked event, so a completed acquisition counts regardless of a change in price."}, {"part": "Signing the acquisition agreement as a separate milestone.", "why": "The item already describes the acquisition as agreed, leaving completion as the tracked outstanding event."}, {"part": "The proposed check date of 24 March 2028.", "why": "The binding-obligation rule requires assessment at the next annual filing for an obligation already taken on, using the supplied February 2027 filing window."}, {"part": "Delay or termination as separately judged outcomes.", "why": "Termination can rule out completion, while delay without completion or termination remains the residual event outcome rather than a separate tracked event."}, {"part": "Purchase-price and goodwill amounts disclosed in quarterly or annual filings.", "why": "These disclosures may establish completion, but their amounts are not the tracked outcome."}], "event": {"happened": "NVIDIA discloses in a completion announcement, Form 8-K or quarterly or annual filing published by 28 February 2027 that its acquisition of Hugging Face has closed.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "NVIDIA, Hugging Face, or a competent regulator or court", "decision": "After 25 September 2026, NVIDIA or Hugging Face formally terminates or abandons the acquisition, or a competent regulator or court issues a final decision prohibiting the acquisition as a whole."}}, "figure": null, "reference": {"words": "The company also recently agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion to expand its software capabilities.", "kind": "expected", "value": "12900000000", "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2027-02-28", "due_day_basis": "stated"}, "passage": "The company also recently agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion to expand its software capabilities."}
{"item": 23, "topic": {"description": "Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology formally approve purchases of Nvidia's new RTX Pro 5500 high-end GPU by Alibaba, ByteDance and other Chinese firms by the end of Nvidia's fiscal 2027, allowing those sales to proceed?", "outcome": "Whether MIIT moves from signaling intent and collecting purchase plans to actually approving Alibaba's, ByteDance's and other Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500 (versus blocking, delaying or capping quantities), so that Nvidia can ship the product into China and book related revenue.", "period": "NVIDIA fiscal year ending late January 2027 — the current fiscal year-end used as the check date for a pending regulatory decision per section 3, because the item gives no date of its own.", "settled_by": "Official MIIT approval decisions or Chinese government announcements on RTX Pro 5500 purchases, confirmed customer orders/shipments, and Nvidia's quarterly China revenue disclosures and FY2027 Form 10-K."}, "answer": {"question": "Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology formally approve Chinese firms' purchases of Nvidia's RTX Pro 5500 GPU, including purchases by Alibaba and ByteDance, by January 31, 2027?", "object": "chip-export-controls", "not_judged": [{"part": "Signaling intent and collecting purchase plans", "why": "These are preliminary regulatory steps, not the formal purchase approval tracked by the topic."}, {"part": "Approval with quantity caps or other conditions versus unrestricted approval", "why": "Restrictions attached to an approval do not constitute a separate outcome because the tracked event is formal approval itself."}, {"part": "Blocking versus delaying purchases", "why": "These are possible paths without approval rather than additional tracked events, and delay alone does not rule approval out."}, {"part": "Allowing Nvidia's sales to proceed, shipping the product into China and booking related revenue", "why": "Actual sales, shipments and recognized revenue are downstream commercial outcomes rather than the regulatory approval being tracked."}], "event": {"happened": "By January 31, 2027, MIIT has formally approved Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500, including purchases by Alibaba and ByteDance, as established by official MIIT decisions or Chinese government announcements; approval with quantity caps or other conditions counts.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology", "decision": "After September 27, 2026, MIIT formally prohibits Chinese firms from purchasing the RTX Pro 5500 or formally abandons the proposed purchase authorization as a whole."}}, "figure": null, "reference": {"words": "the ministry told some of the firms it intends to approve the purchases", "kind": "expected", "value": null, "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2027-01-31", "due_day_basis": "period_end"}, "passage": "the ministry told some of the firms it intends to approve the purchases"}
