{"item": 27, "topic": {"description": "Will Nvidia's Rubin data center GPU — the next generation of the product that carries Nvidia's data center revenue — reach volume ramp in the quarter management describes, or slip into calendar 2027 because of memory shortages?", "outcome": "Whether Rubin's volume ramp and shipments occur in the quarter Nvidia describes (about 20% of data center revenue) or are pushed into calendar 2027, and whether reported sales timing slips.", "period": "Check date: Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report (~November 2026) and fiscal Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027), which will show whether the Rubin ramp landed by the quarter ending late January 2027 or slid into calendar 2027, the two points the item frames ('this quarter' versus 'slip into 2027').", "settled_by": "Nvidia's quarterly revenue-mix and shipment disclosures in its fiscal Q3 and Q4 FY2027 earnings releases and calls, plus confirmed Rubin system shipments by server OEMs/ODMs."}, "answer": {"question": "Will Nvidia's Rubin data center GPU reach commercial volume shipments by January 31, 2027, as confirmed by Nvidia's public disclosures or confirmed server OEM/ODM shipment disclosures available by that date?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue this quarter.", "why": "The tracked outcome is the shipment ramp, not a quarterly revenue-mix figure."}, {"part": "Reaching volume ramp in the particular quarter management describes.", "why": "The question uses the topic's explicit late-January checkpoint rather than separately judging whether shipments began in management's originally described quarter."}, {"part": "The ramp slipping into calendar 2027.", "why": "This is not a separate outcome because January 2027 falls within the topic's stated fiscal-quarter deadline."}, {"part": "Memory shortages causing a delay.", "why": "The question judges whether volume shipments occur, not the cause of any delay."}, {"part": "Reported sales timing slipping.", "why": "Revenue recognition timing is a separate outcome from the commencement of commercial volume shipments."}], "event": {"happened": "By January 31, 2027, Nvidia publicly confirms that Rubin has entered commercial volume shipments, or server OEM/ODM disclosures confirm volume shipments of Rubin systems to customers; announcements of future availability, sampling, or qualification shipments alone do not qualify.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia", "decision": "After October 7, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels Rubin's commercial launch or decides to defer all commercial volume shipments until after January 31, 2027."}}, "figure": null, "reference": {"words": "Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter, and industry reports say the ramp could slip into 2027 because of memory shortages.", "kind": "expected", "value": null, "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2027-01-31", "due_day_basis": "period_end"}, "passage": "Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter, and industry reports say the ramp could slip into 2027 because of memory shortages."}
