hether reported sales timing slips.", "why": "Revenue-recognition timing is distinct from the tracked shipment-ramp event."}, {"part": "The fiscal Q3 FY2027 report as an interim checkpoint.", "why": "That report can provide evidence, but it is not a separately judged event."}], "event": {"happened": "By February 28, 2027, Nvidia's earnings disclosures or confirmed server OEM/ODM shipment disclosures establish that Rubin entered volume production and commercial customer shipments no later than January 31, 2027; engineering samples, demonstrations and pilot shipments alone do not qualify.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia", "decision": "After October 7, 2026, and by February 28, 2027, Nvidia formally cancels Rubin's commercial rollout or decides to defer all Rubin commercial volume shipments until after January 31, 2027."}}, "figure": null, "reference": {"words": "Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter", "kind": "expected", "value": "20", "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2027-02-28", "due_day_basis": "stated"}, "passage": "Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter"}
{"item": 50, "topic": {"description": "Will Nvidia's Groq 3 LPX rack-scale LPU system — the first product built on the Groq technology it paid about $20 billion to license and staff — reach volume shipments and commercial scale in the quarter Nvidia describes (its fiscal Q3 FY2027), or slip?", "outcome": "Whether Groq 3 LPX volume shipments occur 'later this quarter' as Nvidia stated, and whether the system begins contributing to reported data center revenue or slips into fiscal Q4 FY2027/calendar 2027.", "period": "Check date: Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report (~November 2026) confirming shipments in the quarter Nvidia described in the Oct. 8, 2026 item; if unconfirmed there, the fiscal Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027) fixes the slip.", "settled_by": "Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 quarterly report and earnings call (product shipment and revenue disclosure for Groq 3 LPX), plus any shipment/availability confirmation from Nvidia or its system partners."}, "answer": {"question": "Did Nvidia begin volume shipments of Groq 3 LPX during fiscal Q3 FY2027 (August–October 2026), as confirmed by its Q3 report and earnings call or shipment confirmations from Nvidia or its system partners available by November 30, 2026?", "object": "NVDA", "not_judged": [{"part": "Reaching commercial scale", "why": "Commercial scale beyond the start of volume shipments is a separate outcome without a defined threshold in the topic."}, {"part": "Beginning to contribute to reported Data Center revenue", "why": "Revenue contribution is a separate outcome from the tracked start of volume shipments."}, {"part": "Slipping into fiscal Q4 FY2027 or calendar 2027, with follow-up confirmation in the Q4 report", "why": "The question judges whether shipments began in the promised quarter, not the subsequent shipment date or confirmation of that date in a later report."}], "event": {"happened": "Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report or earnings call, or a shipment confirmation from Nvidia or its system partners available by November 30, 2026, confirms that Groq 3 LPX volume shipments began during fiscal Q3 FY2027; production readiness or sample shipments alone do not qualify.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia", "decision": "After October 8, 2026, Nvidia formally abandons the Groq 3 LPX volume-shipment launch or decides to defer the start of all volume shipments until after fiscal Q3 FY2027."}}, "figure": null, "reference": {"words": "volume shipments expected later this quarter", "kind": "expected", "value": null, "value_to": null}, "due_day": "2026-11-30", "due_day_basis": "stated"}, "passage": "volume shipments expected later this quarter"}
