{"i": 22, "t": {"description": "Will NVIDIA complete its approximately $12.9 billion acquisition of Hugging Face, agreed in 2026, by the check date?", "outcome": "Whether the agreed ~$12.9 billion Hugging Face acquisition is signed and closed (completed) as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings, versus being repriced, delayed past the check date or terminated.", "period": "Check date 24 March 2028 (18 months after the 25 September 2026 item) — set per section 3 for a sized acquisition not yet completed, because the item gives no signing or closing date; also observable in NVIDIA's quarterly filings before then.", "settled_by": "NVIDIA's Form 8-K/press release announcing completion (or termination) of the Hugging Face acquisition, and the purchase-price and goodwill disclosures in its Form 10-Q/10-K."}, "q": "Will NVIDIA have completed its agreed acquisition of Hugging Face by 28 February 2027, as established by its completion announcement, Form 8-K or quarterly or annual filings?", "n": ["The approximately $12.9 billion purchase price and whether the acquisition is repriced.", "Signing the acquisition agreement as a separate milestone.", "The proposed check date of 24 March 2028.", "Delay or termination as separately judged outcomes.", "Purchase-price and goodwill amounts disclosed in quarterly or annual filings."], "e": {"happened": "NVIDIA discloses in a completion announcement, Form 8-K or quarterly or annual filing published by 28 February 2027 that its acquisition of Hugging Face has closed.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "NVIDIA, Hugging Face, or a competent regulator or court", "decision": "After 25 September 2026, NVIDIA or Hugging Face formally terminates or abandons the acquisition, or a competent regulator or court issues a final decision prohibiting the acquisition as a whole."}}, "f": null, "d": "2027-02-28", "p": "The company also recently agreed to acquire Hugging Face for approximately $12.9 billion to expand its software capabilities."}
{"i": 23, "t": {"description": "Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology formally approve purchases of Nvidia's new RTX Pro 5500 high-end GPU by Alibaba, ByteDance and other Chinese firms by the end of Nvidia's fiscal 2027, allowing those sales to proceed?", "outcome": "Whether MIIT moves from signaling intent and collecting purchase plans to actually approving Alibaba's, ByteDance's and other Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500 (versus blocking, delaying or capping quantities), so that Nvidia can ship the product into China and book related revenue.", "period": "NVIDIA fiscal year ending late January 2027 — the current fiscal year-end used as the check date for a pending regulatory decision per section 3, because the item gives no date of its own.", "settled_by": "Official MIIT approval decisions or Chinese government announcements on RTX Pro 5500 purchases, confirmed customer orders/shipments, and Nvidia's quarterly China revenue disclosures and FY2027 Form 10-K."}, "q": "Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology formally approve Chinese firms' purchases of Nvidia's RTX Pro 5500 GPU, including purchases by Alibaba and ByteDance, by January 31, 2027?", "n": ["Signaling intent and collecting purchase plans", "Approval with quantity caps or other conditions versus unrestricted approval", "Blocking versus delaying purchases", "Allowing Nvidia's sales to proceed, shipping the product into China and booking related revenue"], "e": {"happened": "By January 31, 2027, MIIT has formally approved Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500, including purchases by Alibaba and ByteDance, as established by official MIIT decisions or Chinese government announcements; approval with quantity caps or other conditions counts.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology", "decision": "After September 27, 2026, MIIT formally prohibits Chinese firms from purchasing the RTX Pro 5500 or formally abandons the proposed purchase authorization as a whole."}}, "f": null, "d": "2027-01-31", "p": "the ministry told some of the firms it intends to approve the purchases"}
{"i": 24, "t": {"description": "How many gigawatts of new data-center capacity will be added in the United States in calendar 2026?", "outcome": "US data-center capacity additions in gigawatts for calendar 2026, versus the pace of 'somewhere between 10, 20 gigawatts a year' that Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang described, and against how far labour availability constrains that pace.", "period": "Calendar year 2026 — the item's present-tense annual pace in a 30 September 2026 article; checked against full-year 2026 grid-operator/interconnection and industry data-center capacity data (expected early 2027).", "settled_by": "Grid operators' and utilities' large-load interconnection and capacity data, EIA electric power data, and the semi-annual industry data-center capacity reports (e.g., CBRE/JLL North America Data Center Trends, Dell'Oro) covering calendar 2026."}, "q": "How many gigawatts of new data-center capacity will be added in the United States during calendar 2026, as established by full-year grid-operator and utility capacity data, EIA electric power data, and industry data-center capacity reports covering 2026?", "n": ["Comparison with Huang's stated pace of 10–20 gigawatts a year.", "How far labour availability constrains the pace of capacity additions."], "e": null, "f": {"unit": "GW", "year": "2026", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "5"}, {"lo": "5", "hi": "10"}, {"lo": "10", "hi": "21"}, {"lo": "21", "hi": "30"}, {"lo": "30", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "n/a", "favourable_why": ""}, "d": "2027-03-31", "p": "somewhere between 10, 20 gigawatts a year"}
{"i": 25, "t": {"description": "Will Nvidia finalize its proposed sharing of up to $125 billion in risk by guaranteeing hardware residual values for its AI infrastructure financing platform by the check date?", "outcome": "Whether the proposed up-to-$125 billion hardware residual-value guarantee is signed and disclosed, and at what amount, versus remaining a proposal or being reduced or withdrawn.", "period": "Check date 3 April 2028 (18 months after the 3 October 2026 item), with earlier disclosure possible in Nvidia's quarterly or annual filings.", "settled_by": "Nvidia's definitive agreement or SEC filing (10-Q/10-K) disclosing the finalized residual-value guarantee amount and terms for its AI infrastructure financing platform."}, "q": "Will Nvidia have signed and disclosed a definitive hardware residual-value guarantee for its AI infrastructure financing platform by 3 April 2028, as evidenced by its definitive agreement or an SEC 10-Q or 10-K filing?", "n": ["The finalized guarantee amount, including whether it is reduced relative to the proposed ceiling of $125 billion.", "The guarantee's detailed terms."], "e": {"happened": "By 3 April 2028, Nvidia has signed a definitive hardware residual-value guarantee for its AI infrastructure financing platform and disclosed it through a definitive agreement or an SEC 10-Q or 10-K filing, regardless of the finalized amount.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia", "decision": "After 3 October 2026 and by 3 April 2028, Nvidia formally abandons or withdraws the proposed hardware residual-value guarantee for its AI infrastructure financing platform as a whole."}}, "f": null, "d": "2028-04-03", "p": "Nvidia also proposed sharing up to $125 billion in risk by guaranteeing hardware residual values."}
{"i": 26, "t": {"description": "How much will Nvidia's maximum potential guarantee liability under the SB Energy/OpenAI affiliate infrastructure leases be at its next annual report?", "outcome": "The maximum potential amount guaranteed, any amounts paid or accrued, and the remaining term of the guarantees disclosed in Nvidia's next annual report.", "period": "Nvidia's next annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027), as fixed by the reason for an obligation already undertaken.", "settled_by": "Nvidia's next annual report (Form 10-K), including the guarantees note and any disclosure of payments or accruals."}, "q": "What maximum potential amount, in USD, will Nvidia report as guaranteed under the SB Energy/OpenAI affiliate infrastructure leases at FY2027 year-end, as disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K guarantees note?", "n": ["Amounts paid under the guarantees", "Amounts accrued under the guarantees", "Remaining term of the guarantees"], "e": null, "f": {"unit": "USD", "year": "FY2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "50000000000"}, {"lo": "50000000000", "hi": "90000000000"}, {"lo": "90000000000", "hi": "110000000000"}, {"lo": "110000000000", "hi": "130000000000"}, {"lo": "130000000000", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "lower", "favourable_why": "A lower maximum guaranteed amount reduces Nvidia's contingent payment exposure if specified tenant defaults occur."}, "d": "2027-02-28", "p": "Nvidia's latest quarterly filing also disclosed guarantees signed in August, capped at $105 billion, supporting an OpenAI affiliate's infrastructure with SB Energy."}
{"i": 27, "t": {"description": "Will Nvidia's Rubin data center GPU — the next generation of the product that carries Nvidia's data center revenue — reach volume ramp in the quarter management describes, or slip into calendar 2027 because of memory shortages?", "outcome": "Whether Rubin's volume ramp and shipments occur in the quarter Nvidia describes (about 20% of data center revenue) or are pushed into calendar 2027, and whether reported sales timing slips.", "period": "Check date: Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report (~November 2026) and fiscal Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027), which will show whether the Rubin ramp landed by the quarter ending late January 2027 or slid into calendar 2027, the two points the item frames ('this quarter' versus 'slip into 2027').", "settled_by": "Nvidia's quarterly revenue-mix and shipment disclosures in its fiscal Q3 and Q4 FY2027 earnings releases and calls, plus confirmed Rubin system shipments by server OEMs/ODMs."}, "q": "Will Nvidia's Rubin data center GPU reach commercial volume shipments by January 31, 2027, as confirmed by Nvidia's public disclosures or confirmed server OEM/ODM shipment disclosures available by that date?", "n": ["Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue this quarter.", "Reaching volume ramp in the particular quarter management describes.", "The ramp slipping into calendar 2027.", "Memory shortages causing a delay.", "Reported sales timing slipping."], "e": {"happened": "By January 31, 2027, Nvidia publicly confirms that Rubin has entered commercial volume shipments, or server OEM/ODM disclosures confirm volume shipments of Rubin systems to customers; announcements of future availability, sampling, or qualification shipments alone do not qualify.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia", "decision": "After October 7, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels Rubin's commercial launch or decides to defer all commercial volume shipments until after January 31, 2027."}}, "f": null, "d": "2027-01-31", "p": "Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter, and industry reports say the ramp could slip into 2027 because of memory shortages."}

