ts until after fiscal Q4 FY2027."}}, "f": null, "d": "2027-02-28", "p": "Its newest chip, Rubin, should make up only about 20% of data center revenue this quarter"}
{"i": 39, "t": {"description": "Will Nvidia's Groq 3 LPX rack-scale LPU system — the first product built on the Groq technology it paid about $20 billion to license and staff — reach volume shipments and commercial scale in the quarter Nvidia describes (its fiscal Q3 FY2027), or slip?", "outcome": "Whether Groq 3 LPX volume shipments occur 'later this quarter' as Nvidia stated, and whether the system begins contributing to reported data center revenue or slips into fiscal Q4 FY2027/calendar 2027.", "period": "Check date: Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report (~November 2026) confirming shipments in the quarter Nvidia described in the Oct. 8, 2026 item; if unconfirmed there, the fiscal Q4 FY2027 report (~February 2027) fixes the slip.", "settled_by": "Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 quarterly report and earnings call (product shipment and revenue disclosure for Groq 3 LPX), plus any shipment/availability confirmation from Nvidia or its system partners."}, "q": "Did Nvidia's Groq 3 LPX rack-scale LPU system begin volume shipments during fiscal Q3 FY2027, as confirmed by Nvidia's quarterly report, earnings call, or Nvidia or system-partner shipment disclosures available by November 30, 2026?", "n": ["Reaching commercial scale beyond the start of volume shipments.", "Beginning to contribute to reported Data Center revenue.", "Whether delayed shipments begin in fiscal Q4 FY2027 or calendar 2027.", "The approximately $20 billion spent licensing Groq technology and hiring its staff."], "e": {"happened": "Nvidia's fiscal Q3 FY2027 report or earnings call, or a shipment disclosure from Nvidia or a system partner available by November 30, 2026, confirms that Groq 3 LPX volume shipments began during fiscal Q3 FY2027; full production, orders, or samples alone do not qualify.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "Nvidia", "decision": "After October 8, 2026, and by November 30, 2026, Nvidia formally cancels the Groq 3 LPX launch or decides to defer all initial volume shipments until after fiscal Q3 FY2027."}}, "f": null, "d": "2026-11-30", "p": "volume shipments expected later this quarter"}
{"i": 40, "t": {"description": "What will the hourly spot rental price for Nvidia B200 GPUs be at the end of calendar 2026, after more than doubling from March 2026 to October 2026?", "outcome": "The hourly spot rental price for Nvidia B200 GPUs at year-end 2026 and whether it remains above its March 2026 level.", "period": "Calendar 2026, settled by Ornn's published GPU rental index releases through year-end 2026 (the Oct. 10, 2026 article gives the March-to-October 2026 move).", "settled_by": "Ornn's published hourly GPU rental index for Nvidia B200 chips, including its releases through year-end 2026."}, "q": "What will the hourly spot rental price for an Nvidia B200 GPU be at calendar year-end 2026, in USD per GPU-hour, as measured by the last 2026 observation in Ornn's published GPU rental index?", "n": ["Whether the year-end 2026 price remains above its March 2026 level.", "The price more than doubling between March and October 2026."], "e": null, "f": {"unit": "other", "year": "2026", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "2"}, {"lo": "2", "hi": "4"}, {"lo": "4", "hi": "6"}, {"lo": "6", "hi": "8"}, {"lo": "8", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "n/a", "favourable_why": ""}, "d": "2027-01-15", "p": null}
{"i": 41, "t": {"description": "What total of credit support and minimum-revenue guarantees to AI labs and cloud partners will NVIDIA disclose at its next annual report?", "outcome": "The disclosed amount of guarantees, credit-support commitments and revenue backstops NVIDIA has extended to AI labs and cloud partners (including the credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity for one additional AI lab), versus the equity investments it has made, at NVIDIA's next annual report.", "period": "Fiscal 2027 annual report (fiscal year ending late January 2027; Form 10-K expected around February 2027) — set as the next annual report following this 22 September 2026 item, per section 3 (obligation already undertaken tracked by its amount at the next annual report; the additional AI lab's credit support is not yet signed and is checked within 18 months).", "settled_by": "NVIDIA's Form 10-K for fiscal 2027 (guarantees, commitments and contingencies note) and any 8-K or earnings disclosure quantifying the credit support for the additional AI lab's ~2 GW of computing capacity and the minimum-revenue guarantees to cloud partners."}, "q": "What total amount, in USD, of outstanding guarantees, credit-support commitments and minimum-revenue backstops extended to AI labs and cloud partners will NVIDIA disclose for its FY2027 year-end in its FY2027 Form 10-K commitments and contingencies disclosures, supplemented by any accompanying 8-K or earnings disclosures quantifying those obligations?", "n": ["The comparison with NVIDIA's equity investments.", "Nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity for the additional AI lab.", "Whether NVIDIA signs the additional AI lab's credit-support arrangement within 18 months."], "e": null, "f": {"unit": "USD", "year": "FY2027", "ranges": [{"lo": null, "hi": "5000000000"}, {"lo": "5000000000", "hi": "15000000000"}, {"lo": "15000000000", "hi": "30000000000"}, {"lo": "30000000000", "hi": "50000000000"}, {"lo": "50000000000", "hi": null}], "favourable_end": "lower", "favourable_why": "Lower obligations reduce NVIDIA's contingent financial exposure, while the item describes both demand benefits and financing risks without establishing that greater commitments are better."}, "d": "2027-02-28", "p": null}
{"i": 42, "t": {"description": "Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform, which the company says has entered full production, reach volume customer shipments (first revenue recognition) by the end of fiscal 2027?", "outcome": "Whether Vera Rubin moves from full production to volume customer shipments and first revenue recognition within NVIDIA's fiscal 2027, as shown in the company's quarterly results and Form 10-K.", "period": "NVIDIA fiscal year ending late January 2027 (FY2027), checked at NVIDIA's quarterly results and FY2027 Form 10-K. The item gives no shipment date; the current fiscal year-end following the September 2026 report that Vera Rubin entered full production is used as the check date.", "settled_by": "NVIDIA quarterly earnings releases and Form 10-K/10-Q disclosures showing Vera Rubin shipments and revenue timing."}, "q": "Will NVIDIA begin volume customer shipments of Vera Rubin, marked by first revenue recognition, during FY2027 ending January 31, 2027, as evidenced by NVIDIA's earnings releases and Form 10-K/10-Q disclosures?", "n": ["Vera Rubin has entered full production."], "e": {"happened": "NVIDIA begins commercial customer shipments of Vera Rubin with first revenue recognition during FY2027, on or before January 31, 2027, as established by its earnings releases or SEC disclosures; production alone or shipments without revenue recognition do not qualify.", "ruled_out": {"by_whom": "NVIDIA", "decision": "After September 23, 2026, NVIDIA formally cancels Vera Rubin's commercialization or decides to defer all revenue-recognized customer shipments until after FY2027."}}, "f": null, "d": "2027-01-31", "p": null}
